C.1 Proof of Theorem 1.1 (Core Safety Guarantee)

Statement. Under assumptions A1–A8, the ZENITH system \mathcal{Z} satisfies for all traces t:

\neg \text{UnauthorizedAction}_\Earth(t) \land \text{OrbitalNonInfluence}_\Earth(t).

Proof. The two conjuncts are proved separately.

1. No unauthorized terrestrial action: By Theorem 1.4 (constraint soundness), any execution trace respects \mathcal{I}_{\text{HW}}. An unauthorized action would be an exec(a) that occurs without a valid license token or in excess of resource caps. But \mathcal{I}_{\text{HW}} includes tokens > 0 for any exec(a) transition, and the license validation (Theorem 1.8) ensures that only properly signed and valid licenses can increase tokens. Hence no such action can occur.
2. Orbital non‑influence: This is the content of Theorem 1.3, proved in Appendix C.2.

The conjunction follows. ∎

