C.7 Proof of Theorem 1.8 (License Validation Correctness)

Statement. validate_license(lic) returns .valid iff all six conditions hold.

Proof. The function is defined by a sequence of guard clauses. By structural induction on the match syntax:

· If CBOR parsing fails → .struct_invalid; condition (1) fails.
· If signature verification fails → .signature_invalid; condition (2) fails.
· If current time not in validity window → .expired; condition (3) fails.
· If lic.device_id != local_puf → .device_mismatch; condition (4) fails.
· If license is revoked → .revoked; condition (5) fails.
· Otherwise, enforce_policy evaluates the resource limits against the current hardware state. By Lemma enforce_policy_iff_I_HW, enforce_policy returns true exactly when \mathcal{I}_{\text{HW}} holds (condition 6). The function then returns .valid.

The converse direction: if .valid is returned, then all guards passed, so all six conditions hold. The proof is a direct case analysis, formally mechanisable in Lean 4. ∎

