E.1 System Overview

The ZENITH architecture enforces existential AI safety by physically separating computation with epistemic authority (analysis, prediction) from computation with executive authority (action, control). The separation is achieved through:

· A space‑based constellation (Ω) that performs only passive analysis.
· A hardware enforcement layer (Η) on Earth that enforces resource bounds and mediates all commands.
· A terrestrial agent ecosystem (E) that executes actions only when authorised by a cryptographically signed license.

All communication is unidirectional in terms of authority flow: Orbital data cannot directly trigger terrestrial action. Human governance is inserted as a mandatory step for license issuance.

