· State transfer: If a node falls behind, it requests a checkpoint from 2f+1 peers to recover safely.

Security under partial synchrony: Safety is guaranteed unconditionally; liveness is temporarily lost during asynchronous periods but resumes after GST. The physical orbital geometry ensures GST is reached within bounded time after any transient link failure.

